{
  "id": "sensory-modulation-dysfunction",
  "term": "sensory modulation dysfunction",
  "definition": "Sensory modulation dysfunction is a type of sensory processing disorder in which one or more sensory systems do not regulate responses to input in a flexible, graded way. It can involve over-responsiveness, where ordinary non-painful sensations feel unusually unpleasant or painful, and/or under-responsiveness, where reactions to sensory input are reduced, and it can interfere with daily activities, work, and quality of life.",
